 "intro_text": "In books and documents, a section is a subdivision, especially of a chapter.\nIn fiction, sections often represent scenes, and accordingly the space separating them is sometimes also called a scene break. Scene breaks represent gaps in story time that do not correspond to discourse time, and thus reveal the story-discourse distinction.\nIn law, sections are divisions of legislation that may be deeply nested to as little as single sentences.",
